-----> Waterfall Model :
------------------------
-Oldest SDLC Model.
-It is also Known as the LInear Sequential Model.
-In this model , each Phase must be completed before the next phase can begin and there is no overlapping of phases.i.e all the phases will be performed
one by one just like flowing of water fall downwards.

Advantages :
-------------
-simple and easy to implement.
-phases won't be overlapped thereby no ambiguity.
-all the phases will be executed one by one it gives high visibility to the project managers and clients about the progress of the project.
-best suitable for the requirements are fixed.
-best suitable for small projects.

Disadvantages :
---------------
-It is very rigid model because it won't accept requirements changes in the middle.
-client satisfaction is very low because most of the times client will add new requirements in the middle ,which won't be supported.
-total projects development time is more because testing should be done after completing development only.
-cost of bug fixing is very high because we can not identify bugs in the early stage of life cycle.
-not suitable if the requirements keep on changing.
-not suitable for large projects.




