Agile Model :
--------------
This is the most frequent used and hot cake model for S/W Development.
Agile Model is divided into several sub models.
   1)Rational Unify process(RUP)
   2)Adaptive S/W Development 
   3)Feature driven Dev(FDD)
   4)Crystal clear
   5)Dynamic S/W dev model(DSDM)
   6)Extreme Programming 
   7)Scrum etc..


Scrum :
--------
Among all these models , Scrum model is the most popular & most frequently used one , it is derived from Rugby game.
-it is light weight process .
-it is an iterative /incremental model and it accept the changes in the middle easily.
-it is people based model but not plan based.
team collaboration and continuous feedback are strengths of this model.

-->Scrum model is not linear sequential model,it is a iterative model
-->total S/W will be developed increment/increment and each increment is called a sprint .
-->Sprint is a deliverable/shippable product in scrum model.
    ->scrum model follows increment by increment.
    ->each increment will take one to 3 weeks duration.
    ->7 to 9 members are responsible in every sprint.
-->The art of doing twice work in half time is nothing but scrum model.

Advantages :
-------------
-there is maximum chance for quality.
-it ensures effective use of time and money.
-client satisfaction is very high because it accept requirement changes in the middle.
-there is a possibility for the client involvement in every stage of project development.
-project status tracking is very easy .
-Team gets complete visibility through Scrum meetings.

Limitations of Scrum :
------------------------
-the chances of project failure is very high if individuals are not committed or cooperative.
-Adaptive scrum model for large projects is very big challenge.
-It must required experienced and efficient team members.
-if any team member leaves in the middle of project , it can have a huge negative impact on the project.


